# A duplicate key stays an error even in a non-strict mode, it is not
# one of the errors sql_mode downgrades to a warning. Only IGNORE would
# make the remote server skip the row, and an IGNORE statement is not
# pushed down at all, see the section on the statements that stay local
CALL fill_tables();
UPDATE t3, t2 SET t3.b= 30 WHERE t3.a= t2.a AND t3.a < 3;
ERROR 23000: Duplicate entry '30' for key 'b'
